# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Report Log captures — runtime output of the "Report Log" switch, written INSIDE the
# integration folder by design (owner's decision, see const.py's REPORT LOG section).
# User data, never repository content.
reports/

# Editor / workspace files (personal preference, not project content)
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# OS
.DS_Store

# Safety net: nothing currently matches these, checked recursively before
# adding this file, but keep them ignored by default going forward.
*.env
.env
*token*
*credential*
*secret*

# Session handoffs — deliberately NOT published.
#
# These are working notes for continuing the project, not documentation anyone else can use,
# and they carry the owner's email and the hub's LAN address. They live here rather than
# outside the repo so every doc pointer and every session's habits keep working; they are
# simply never committed. Purged from history 2026-08-20, before the first push.
#
# ⚠️ They are the project's memory. Back them up separately — git is not doing it.
docs/handoff/

# Agent/owner working layer — deliberately NOT published, purged from history 2026-08-20.
#
# `CLAUDE.md` is Claude Code's project-instructions file and `intro.md` is the orientation
# document it points at. Both describe *this machine* — the Home Assistant add-on container,
# the venv at /homeassistant/scripts/kohler-work, which restart does what — and would mislead
# anyone who cloned the repo, since none of those paths exist for them. They also name the
# owner. Nothing published links to either; the protocol content they summarise lives in
# docs/ where it belongs.
#
# ⚠️ Like docs/handoff/, git is not backing these up.
CLAUDE.md
intro.md

# Agent working layer — deliberately NOT published, same category as CLAUDE.md / intro.md.
#
# `.claude/agents/` holds the subagent definitions this project delegates to. They describe
# *this machine* — /homeassistant/kohler_konnect_raw, the kohler-work venv,
# `tests/run_offline.sh` — none of which exist for anyone who clones this repo, so shipping
# them would mislead rather than help.
#
# ⚠️ Like docs/handoff/, git is not backing these up.
.claude/

# HACS default-store submission checklist — working notes, deliberately NOT published.
#
# `docs/hacs-submission.md` is a checklist for getting this repository into the HACS default
# store: what is already satisfied, the exact PR to open, and the queue timings measured from
# the hacs/default API. It is process, not product — it documents *our* submission rather
# than anything a user of the integration needs, and it carries links to specific Actions
# runs that mean nothing to anyone else.
#
# ⚠️ Like docs/handoff/, git is not backing this up.
docs/hacs-submission.md
